- imgui/: still contains debugger-client.js, imgui-debugger.js, poc.js, source-view.js,
  target.js, transport.js, var-tree.js, wire-codec.js even though commit 53c6812 removed
  the classes already implemented in the top-level *.js files. Per gui/PLAN.md, imgui/ is
  "not used or touched" by the supported GUI (gui/), so it's unclear which of these
  remaining files are still needed vs. leftover from the earlier prototype.
- installed-qjs-is-i386: /usr/local/bin/qjs is a 32-bit (i686) build linked against /usr/local/lib/i386-linux-gnu/libquickjs.so, so
  qjs-debugger (debuggee qjs) runs on an engine without the patches/008 fixes, and an earlier "r" in the repl
  killed it with SIGSEGV (the `print` crash). qjsm is x86-64 and fine. Reinstall a 64-bit qjs.
- server-late-client: a WebSocket client that connects after the engine reached its entry stop never sees that
  StoppedEvent (broadcast to nobody); it has to assume the stop and send continue/breakpoints blindly.
- process-rejection-tracker: an unhandled promise rejection under the installed qjsm prints "TypeError: not a
  function at rejection (qjs-modules/lib/process.js)" instead of the rejection; found while debugging the
  library API, avoided there by keeping send errors handled (engine-connection.js attachSession).
- info-locals-exception: `info locals` lists an `<exception>` pseudo variable ("[unsupported type]" when none is pending).
